# A trait's default body is a body of a method the trait signs, as an impl's method is
# (`^Box` has no method `Other`), and its clauses are one definition: a second clause the
# first already takes is never reached (Type System ch. 3: "An impl gives each method its
# definition lines"). Written by Claude on the claude-bugs branch; subject to change.
trait ^Shape a:
    Area: fn a -> Nat
    fn Area x = 1
    fn Area x = 2
    fn Extra x = 0
